# The Worker's secrets, in dotenv format.
#
# Two readers, and the second one is why the values below are EMPTY:
#   • the Deploy to Cloudflare button prompts for each of these at deploy time,
#     PREFILLED WITH THE VALUE IN THIS FILE (descriptions come from package.json
#     `cloudflare.bindings`). A placeholder here is a default there — this file
#     once said `change-me`, which offered every presser a CDN whose session
#     cookie was signed with a string printed in a public repo.
#   • local dev — `cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars`, fill it in, and `wrangler dev`
#     picks it up. .dev.vars is gitignored, and `bun run types` reads it to type
#     env.CDN_* in the generated Env.
#
# On a deployed Worker they are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>` (or in the
# dashboard). ONE of them is required. The rest are provisioned by `cdn setup`,
# and until they exist the paths they guard are CLOSED, never open.

# REQUIRED, and the only thing a one-click deploy asks you for. Anything you'd
# type — it is a password field, so let your password manager generate it. It
# also signs the session cookie unless CDN_SESSION_SECRET is set below, which is
# the other reason to make it a good one.
CDN_PASSWORD=

# OPTIONAL. Bearer for POST /api/upload — the write path used by scripts, the
# CLI, the Claude Code hooks and the macOS Shortcut. Leave blank: with no token
# configured every bearer is rejected, so a fresh CDN has no write path rather
# than an open one, and you can still upload by dragging onto the explorer.
# `cdn setup` generates one and stores it for you when you want the machine path.
CDN_UPLOAD_TOKEN=

# OPTIONAL. Signs the session cookie. Leave blank and the key is derived from
# CDN_PASSWORD, which is what makes the one-field deploy above possible. Set it
# to decouple the two — rotating sessions without changing your password, or the
# reverse:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
CDN_SESSION_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL. A Cloudflare API token scoped to Zone → Cache Purge on your zone and
# nothing else. With it (plus the CDN_ZONE_ID / CDN_PUBLIC_ORIGIN vars in
# wrangler.jsonc) a write invalidates every edge POP, so an overwrite is visible
# immediately worldwide. Leave blank and the purge is local-POP only — the
# fallback, not an error. `cdn setup` mints this one for you.
CDN_PURGE_TOKEN=
